      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        67.21469116210938,
        527.4247436523438,
        81.83369445800781
      ],
      "text": "Delamanid formulations : In the trial, delamanid was dosed with the dispersible 25 mg tablet",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiboldItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        80.59070587158203,
        527.3757934570312,
        95.03370666503906
      ],
      "text": "tested in children aged 3–5 years. Bioavailability of delamanid may be altered when the 50 mg",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        93.79071807861328,
        527.390380859375,
        108.23371887207031
      ],
      "text": "adult tablet is split, crushed or dissolved. There are also concerns that the adult tablet may shatter if",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        106.99073028564453,
        527.4620361328125,
        121.43373107910156
      ],
      "text": "attempts are made to split it, and its contents are exceedingly bitter and unpalatable. The tablets are",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        120.19074249267578,
        527.3881225585938,
        134.6337432861328
      ],
      "text": "susceptible to oxidation and heat; thus, retaining pill fragments for use at any time other than the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        133.3907012939453,
        527.43212890625,
        147.8336944580078
      ],
      "text": "time of administration is likely to result in the delivery of lower-than-expected active compound and",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        146.59071350097656,
        527.39599609375,
        161.03370666503906
      ],
      "text": "unspecified oxidation by-products. The child-friendly formulation of delamanid (25 mg dispersible",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        159.7907257080078,
        527.3790283203125,
        174.2337188720703
      ],
      "text": "tablet, unscored) has been included in the 8th WHO Essential Medicine List for Children (EMLc),",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        170.1967315673828,
        527.4974365234375,
        187.43373107910156
      ],
      "text": "(88) released in October 2021  , was approved by the European Medicines Agency in September 2021",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 10.992648124694824,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        186.1907501220703,
        527.4346313476562,
        200.6337432861328
      ],
      "text": "and has been available through the Stop TB Partnership GDF since October 2021. Children in the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        199.3907012939453,
        527.43115234375,
        213.8336944580078
      ],
      "text": "0–2-year cohort in study 242–12–233 were administered a 5 mg paediatric dispersible formulation",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        212.59071350097656,
        527.4036254882812,
        227.03370666503906
      ],
      "text": "that is not expected to be commercialized. There has been no direct bioequivalence comparison",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        225.7906036376953,
        527.4343872070312,
        240.2335968017578
      ],
      "text": "for the 5 mg paediatric formulation and the 50 mg adult tablet. In a crossover bioequivalence study,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        238.99061584472656,
        527.4287719726562,
        253.43360900878906
      ],
      "text": "neither Cmax [90%CI GMR 0.701,0.809] nor AUC [90%CI GMR 0.775,0.909] satisfied the criteria for",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        252.1906280517578,
        527.5545043945312,
        266.6336364746094
      ],
      "text": "bioequivalence as specified by regulatory agencies. As such, the 5 mg paediatric and the 50 mg adult",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.983086585998535,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        262.59661865234375,
        263.5898742675781,
        279.8336486816406
      ],
      "text": "(96) formulations are not interchangeable  .",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        287.094482421875,
        527.54931640625,
        301.5375061035156
      ],
      "text": "Dosing guidance for the use of delamanid in children below 3 years of age is provided in the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        300.29449462890625,
        527.1901245117188,
        314.7375183105469
      ],
      "text": "operational handbook, based on an expert consultation on dosing that was conducted after the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        313.49462890625,
        527.3927001953125,
        327.9376525878906
      ],
      "text": "GDG meeting. The guidance takes into account the availability of the 25 mg dispersible delamanid",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        326.69451904296875,
        129.32119750976562,
        341.1375427246094
      ],
      "text": "formulation.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        348.2225036621094,
        527.4140014648438,
        362.8415222167969
      ],
      "text": "Administration of delamanid : Bioavailability of delamanid was optimized in the trials by administering",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiboldItalic",
      "size": 10.94486141204834,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        361.5985107421875,
        527.2060546875,
        376.0415344238281
      ],
      "text": "delamanid with a high-fat meal; and therefore administration of delamanid with food is an important",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.994749069213867,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        374.7984924316406,
        527.3826293945312,
        389.24151611328125
      ],
      "text": "aspect to consider for practical implementation. In neonates, there are higher feeding frequencies,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        387.9985046386719,
        399.3338928222656,
        402.4415283203125
      ],
      "text": "which aligns well with the goal of administering with higher-fat content.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        409.702392578125,
        527.41357421875,
        424.1454162597656
      ],
      "text": "Regimen building of longer regimens: Guidance on how to construct optimal treatment regimens",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        422.90240478515625,
        527.4398193359375,
        437.3454284667969
      ],
      "text": "for children with MDR/RR-TB (with drugs based on WHO recommended drug classification as well",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        436.1024169921875,
        527.37939453125,
        450.5454406738281
      ],
      "text": "as optimal treatment duration) who are not eligible for shorter, all-oral regimens is provided in the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        449.3023986816406,
        178.30311584472656,
        463.74542236328125
      ],
      "text": "operational handbook.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        470.8304138183594,
        527.4396362304688,
        485.4494323730469
      ],
      "text": "Duration of treatment : Shortening the total treatment duration to less than 18 months may be",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiboldItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        481.41241455078125,
        527.4763793945312,
        498.6494445800781
      ],
      "text": "(61) considered for children without extensive disease  . Extensive (or advanced) TB disease refers to the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 10.970410346984863,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        497.4064025878906,
        527.390380859375,
        511.84942626953125
      ],
      "text": "presence of bilateral cavitary disease or extensive parenchymal damage on CXR. Severe EPTB refers",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        510.6064453125,
        527.5156860351562,
        525.0494384765625
      ],
      "text": "to the presence of miliary TB or TBM in adolescents and adults over 15 years of age. In children aged",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.99639892578125,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        523.806396484375,
        527.3936157226562,
        538.2493896484375
      ],
      "text": "below 15 years, extrapulmonary forms of disease other than lymphadenopathy (peripheral nodes or",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        534.21240234375,
        499.2709655761719,
        551.4494018554688
      ],
      "text": "(86) isolated mediastinal mass without compression) are considered as severe (adapted from  ).",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        558.5343627929688,
        527.4067993164062,
        573.1533203125
      ],
      "text": "Concurrent use of delamanid and bedaquiline, and use of delamanid beyond six months : With",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiboldItalic",
      "size": 10.995048522949219,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        571.9102783203125,
        527.6116943359375,
        586.353271484375
      ],
      "text": "regards to concurrent delamanid and bedaquiline use, evidence assessed by a GDG in November 2019",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.950287818908691,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        585.1102905273438,
        527.4114379882812,
        599.5532836914062
      ],
      "text": "included new data on concurrent bedaquiline and delamanid use. The new evidence was insufficient",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        598.310302734375,
        527.4497680664062,
        612.7532958984375
      ],
      "text": "to allow the GDG to make a statement about the effectiveness of concurrent use of both medicines.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        611.5103149414062,
        527.44091796875,
        625.9533081054688
      ],
      "text": "However, the group concluded that the safety data assessed in 2019 suggest no additional safety",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        624.7103271484375,
        527.193115234375,
        639.1533203125
      ],
      "text": "concerns with regard to the concurrent use of bedaquiline and delamanid. Therefore, bedaquiline and",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.969657897949219,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        637.9102783203125,
        527.39697265625,
        652.353271484375
      ],
      "text": "delamanid may be used in people with MDR/RR-TB who have limited options for other treatment,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        651.1102905273438,
        527.44775390625,
        665.5532836914062
      ],
      "text": "such as those with few effective drugs that can be included in their regimen, for example due to an",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        664.310302734375,
        527.4255981445312,
        678.7532958984375
      ],
      "text": "extensive drug-resistance profile or intolerance to other second-line TB medications. Appropriate",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        677.5103149414062,
        527.3914184570312,
        691.9533081054688
      ],
      "text": "schedules of safety monitoring (at baseline and throughout treatment) should be in place for these",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        690.7103271484375,
        527.5711059570312,
        705.1533203125
      ],
      "text": "patients, including ECG and electrolyte monitoring, and clinicians should be aware of other medicines",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.985490798950195,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        703.9102783203125,
        527.4518432617188,
        718.353271484375
      ],
      "text": "in the regimen that can either prolong the QT interval or cause other potential adverse events. The",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        717.1102905273438,
        527.424560546875,
        731.5532836914062
      ],
      "text": "available evidence of delamanid use is currently limited to the on-label 6-month duration alongside",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        730.310302734375,
        524.37646484375,
        744.7532958984375
      ],
      "text": "other medicines in a longer regimen; prolongation beyond 6 months can be considered on a case-",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        740.71630859375,
        149.37359619140625,
        757.9533081054688
      ],
      "text": "(9) by-case basis  .",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        344.452392578125,
        801.0170288085938,
        554.0401611328125,
        811.52099609375
      ],
      "text": "5. Treatment of TB disease in children and adolescents 51",
